                <pb facs="1214" n="1102" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg1102"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.5034 (China) Thrift Corp./34: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-07T18:00:00-05:00">October 7, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>15. Your 28, October 5, 1 p.m.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d1061-f1"/> and 29, October
                    6, 3 p.m. The Department is doubtful whether American authorities in China could
                    properly refuse to recognize the jurisdictional status of the bank as an
                    American citizen if that question were submitted for judicial determination.
                    However, the question is primarily one for consideration by the Court and if the
                    Judge of the United States Court for China is prepared to maintain in any
                    possible judicial proceeding the position reported in the final paragraph of
                    your telegram 29, August [<hi rendition="#italic">October</hi>] 6, 3 p.m., the
                    Department would not object to your suggested instruction to Harbin.</p>
                <p>The Department realizes the desirability of avoiding participation by American
                    authorities in the bank liquidation, if that course may properly be taken, but,
                    if the Court should ultimately be required to assume jurisdiction, it would seem
                    preferable that jurisdiction be taken immediately and that all possible measures
                    be adopted to effect the quickest and most equitable adjustment of the bank’s
                    affairs.</p>
                <p>The Department is making inquiry of the Governor of Nevada in regard to the
                    validity of the company’s charter and will inform you of his reply.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
